LTRData fork of libqcow
======================

This is LTRData's fork of libyal/libqcow, a native C library for reading
QEMU Copy-On-Write (QCOW) disk images:
https://github.com/libyal/libqcow

Fork scope and status
---------------------

The main branch contains upstream version 20220429 (April 2022), followed
by LTRData's May 2022 msvcrt.dll compatibility changes. Those changes add
or update Visual C++ projects and property sheets for Windows runtime
compatibility; they do not add QCOW write support.

The library remains read-only. The format-support list and alpha status
below are retained from the upstream README for this snapshot. Its
"work in progress" wording is historical upstream context, not a promise
of ongoing development in this fork. Consult libyal/libqcow for current
upstream development and documentation.

Source layout
--------------

* libqcow and include: native library implementation and public C API.
* qcowtools: qcowinfo for image information and qcowmount for mounting
  image data.
* pyqcow: Python bindings.
* documentation and manuals: format documentation and API/tool manuals.
* msvscpp: Visual C++ solution and projects.

The retained libqcow.nuspec describes native headers and Win32/x64
libraries under the upstream package name libqcow. It is not a managed
.NET wrapper.

Building
--------

The repository includes dependency-synchronization scripts, Autotools
configuration and Windows build scripts. Start with the upstream build
documentation linked below, taking this snapshot and its local project
settings into account.

The Visual C++ configurations use different toolsets. Some import the
LTRData compatibility property sheets, which contain machine-specific
WDK 7 paths and legacy msvcrt runtime objects. Inspect the selected
configuration and adapt those paths for your environment. These settings
do not establish support for every Windows version.

Attribution and license texts are in AUTHORS, COPYING and COPYING.LESSER.
See individual source headers for the terms applicable to each component.

Original upstream README for this snapshot
==========================================

libqcow is a library to access the QEMU Copy-On-Write (QCOW) image format.

Project information:

* Status: alpha
* Licence: LGPLv3+

Read-only supported QCOW formats:

* version 1
* version 2
* version 3

Supported QCOW format features:

* zlib (DEFLATE) compression
* AES-CBC 128-bit encryption
* backing file (differential image)

Unsupported QCOW format features:

* LUKS encryption
* data file
* in-image snapshots

Work in progress:

* Thread-safety in file API functions

For more information see:

* Project documentation: https://github.com/libyal/libqcow/wiki/Home
* How to build from source: https://github.com/libyal/libqcow/wiki/Building

